  The changes amount to nothing less than dismantling an old civilization a
 nd building a new one\, whose newness is often the return of the old ways 
 and wisdoms. In this rising worldview\, interconnection is a core idea and
  value. But because the transformation has happened in so many disparate a
 renas\, and within a longer arc of history\, the scale of that change is s
 eldom recognized. [data-website-component-id="49301595ba476ddf6c43"] { --s
